        {
          "type": "response_end",
          "response": {
            "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent reviews newly published events and organizers on an event ticketing platform. It leaves a recommendation (approve, reject, or request-info) with reasons for a human admin to decide. The agent has graded autonomy: it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it. Offline evals showed significant improvements in fraud detection accuracy when using Claude Haiku 5.5 compared to a local model.",
