                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent reviews newly published events and organizers on an event ticketing platform. It leaves an \"approve / reject / request-info\" recommendation, with reasons, for a human admin. Its graded autonomy means it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, while web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it.\n\nOffline evals showed that on a local 9B model, approved fraud fell from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations, and fraud approved without human review dropped from 27% to 0%. Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen for deployment: it achieved 86% accuracy vs 71%, with only 1% of fraud approved vs 8%. The cost is about $0.002 per review."
